# Phase 1 – Network Reconnaissance and Discovery

## Objective
The objective of this phase is to perform network reconnaissance and establish a baseline understanding of the target environment. This includes identifying live hosts, open ports, operating systems, MAC addresses, and potential vulnerabilities within the network.

## Tools Used
- Python
- Nmap
- ifconfig
- Linux Terminal
- Jupyter Notebook

## Skills Demonstrated
- Network Enumeration
- Port Scanning
- Service Identification
- Operating System Fingerprinting
- Basic Vulnerability Assessment
- Python Automation

## Project Overview
In this phase, network scanning and discovery techniques were performed inside a virtual cybersecurity lab environment using Python automation and Nmap. The project focused on identifying active systems and analyzing exposed services to better understand normal network behavior and possible attack surfaces.

## Key Tasks
- Enumerated live systems on the network
- Collected IP and MAC addresses
- Identified open ports and services
- Analyzed operating systems
- Documented suspicious findings
- Automated portions of reconnaissance using Python

